IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`

-- ccc14-part122-offence.l4 -- PART XII.2 "Proceeds of Crime", ss 462.3 and 462.31 (definitions; laundering proceeds of crime) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`) and, for the one enumeration `s 2 form of the charge` (the offence itself, a conspiracy, an attempt,
-- being an accessory after the fact, counselling), the keel's definitions (`ccc-definitions`); no keel function is called: every answer from another part is an input named for its section.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: JUST TRUE = the text brings the case within the provision; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered (see NOTES.md).

§ `PART XII.2 -- Proceeds of Crime`

§§ `s 462.3 -- Interpretation: Definitions ("In this Part,")`

-- src:7990 | 462.3 (1) In this Part,
-- src:7991 | designated drug offence [Repealed, 1996, c. 19, s. 68]
@ref s 462.3(1) lead-in and "designated drug offence", shown repealed (src:7990-7991)
`s 462.3(1) designated drug offence as the text shows it` MEANS "designated drug offence [Repealed, 1996, c. 19, s. 68]"

-- src:7992 | designated offence means
-- src:7993 | (a) any offence that may be prosecuted as an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, other than an indictable offence prescribed by regulation, or
-- src:7994 | (b) a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in paragraph (a); (infraction désignée)
@ref s 462.3(1) "designated offence" (src:7992-7994)
GIVEN form IS A `s 2 form of the charge`
      `the offence may be prosecuted as an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an indictable offence prescribed by regulation, by the regulations under subsection 462.3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.3(1) designated offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a form of participation that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "designated offence means"
    OTHERWISE   -- the offence itself (a), or a conspiracy, attempt, accessory after the fact or counselling in relation to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) (b)
        IF `the offence may be prosecuted as an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` AND NOT `the offence is an indictable offence prescribed by regulation, by the regulations under subsection 462.3(2)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any offence that may be prosecuted as an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, other than an indictable offence prescribed by regulation"

-- src:7995 | designated substance offence [Repealed, 2001, c. 32, s. 12]
-- src:7996 | enterprise crime offence [Repealed, 2001, c. 32, s. 12]
@ref s 462.3(1) "designated substance offence" and "enterprise crime offence", shown repealed (src:7995-7996)
`s 462.3(1) designated substance offence and enterprise crime offence as the text shows them` MEANS "designated substance offence [Repealed, 2001, c. 32, s. 12]; enterprise crime offence [Repealed, 2001, c. 32, s. 12]"

-- src:7997 | judge means a judge as defined in section 552 or a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction; (juge)
@ref s 462.3(1) "judge" (src:7997)
GIVEN `the person is a judge as defined in section 552, by s 552 judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.3(1) judge` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `the person is a judge as defined in section 552, by s 552 judge`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("judge means"); NOTHING when s 552 "judge" is itself not covered

-- src:7998 | proceeds of crime means any property, benefit or advantage, within or outside Canada, obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of
-- src:7999 | (a) the commission in Canada of a designated offence, or
-- src:8000 | (b) an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted a designated offence. (produits de la criminalité)
@ref s 462.3(1) "proceeds of crime" (src:7998-8000)
GIVEN `it is property, benefit or advantage, within or outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of the commission in Canada of an offence that is a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.3(1) proceeds of crime` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is property, benefit or advantage, within or outside Canada`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "proceeds of crime means any property, benefit or advantage"
    ELSE CONSIDER `it was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of the commission in Canada of an offence that is a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence`
         WHEN JUST a THEN
             IF a
             THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
             ELSE `it was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence`   -- (b): JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("means"); NOTHING when "designated offence" is itself not covered
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `it was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence`
             WHEN JUST b THEN
                 IF b
                 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
                 ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (a)'s offence is a designated offence is itself not covered
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a designated offence is itself not covered

-- src:8002 | (2) The Governor in Council may make regulations prescribing indictable offences that are excluded from the definition designated offence in subsection (1).
-- src:8003 | (3) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 179]
-- src:8004 | (4) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 179]
