`s 462.3(2) to (4) as the text shows them` MEANS "The Governor in Council may make regulations prescribing indictable offences that are excluded from the definition designated offence in subsection (1). (3) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 179] (4) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 179]"

§§ `s 462.31 -- Laundering proceeds of crime`

-- src:8008 | 462.31 (1) Every one commits an offence who uses, transfers the possession of, sends or delivers to any person or place, transports, transmits, alters, disposes of or otherwise deals with, in any manner and by any means, any property or any proceeds of any property with intent to conceal or convert that property or those proceeds, knowing or believing that, or being reckless as to whether, all or a part of that property or of those proceeds was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of
-- src:8009 | (a) the commission in Canada of a designated offence; or
-- src:8010 | (b) an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted a designated offence.
@ref s 462.31(1) (src:8008-8010)
GIVEN `uses, transfers the possession of, sends or delivers to any person or place, transports, transmits, alters, disposes of or otherwise deals with, in any manner and by any means, any property or any proceeds of any property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `with intent to conceal or convert that property or those proceeds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowing or believing that, or being reckless as to whether, all or a part of that property or of those proceeds was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commission in Canada of a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.31(1) the person commits the offence of laundering proceeds of crime` MEANS
    IF `uses, transfers the possession of, sends or delivers to any person or place, transports, transmits, alters, disposes of or otherwise deals with, in any manner and by any means, any property or any proceeds of any property`
        AND `with intent to conceal or convert that property or those proceeds`
        AND `knowing or believing that, or being reckless as to whether, all or a part of that property or of those proceeds was obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of`
        AND (`the commission in Canada of a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
             OR `an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted a designated offence, by s 462.3(1) designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an offence who uses, transfers the possession of, sends or delivers to any person or place, transports, transmits, alters, disposes of or otherwise deals with"

-- src:8011 | (1.1) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 378]
-- src:8012 | (1.2) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 378]
-- src:8013 | (1.3) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 378]
@ref s 462.31(1.1) to (1.3), shown repealed (src:8011-8013)
`s 462.31(1.1) to (1.3) as the text shows them` MEANS "(1.1) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 378] (1.2) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 378] (1.3) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 378]"

-- src:8015 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:8016 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:8017 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 462.31(2) (src:8015-8017)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 462.31(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 462.31(2) (src:8015-8017)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 462.31(2) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (a)
       , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (b)

-- src:8019 | (2.1) Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years.
@ref s 462.31(2.1) (src:8019)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection (1), by s 462.31(1) the person commits the offence of laundering proceeds of crime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.31(2.1) the person commits the offence of laundering proceeds of crime for a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the person commits an offence under subsection (1), by s 462.31(1) the person commits the offence of laundering proceeds of crime` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`
        AND `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization"

@ref s 462.31(2.1) (src:8019)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 462.31(2.1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 462.31(2.1) (src:8019)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 462.31(2.1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

-- src:8021 | (2.2) Subject to subsection (2.4), in a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1) or (2.1), it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that the accused knew, believed they knew or was reckless as to the specific nature of the designated offence.
@ref s 462.31(2.2) (src:8021)
GIVEN `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1) or (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is also charged with the designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.31(2.2) it is necessary for the prosecutor to prove that the accused knew, believed they knew or was reckless as to the specific nature of the designated offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1) or (2.1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1) or (2.1)"
    ELSE IF `the accused is also charged with the designated offence`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (2.4) says (2.2) does not apply, and the text does not say what must then be proved
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that the accused knew, believed they knew or was reckless as to the specific nature of the designated offence"

-- src:8023 | (2.3) Subject to subsection (2.4), the court may infer that an accused had the knowledge or belief or demonstrated the recklessness referred to in subsection (1) if it is satisfied, given the circumstances of the offence, that the manner in which the accused dealt with the property or its proceeds is markedly unusual or the accused’s dealings are inconsistent with lawful activities typical of the sector in which they take place, including business activities.
@ref s 462.31(2.3) (src:8023)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, given the circumstances of the offence, that the manner in which the accused dealt with the property or its proceeds is markedly unusual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied, given the circumstances of the offence, that the accused’s dealings are inconsistent with lawful activities typical of the sector in which they take place, including business activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is also charged with the designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.31(2.3) the court may infer that the accused had the knowledge or belief or demonstrated the recklessness referred to in subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the accused is also charged with the designated offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2.2) and (2.3) do not apply in cases where the accused is also charged with the designated offence"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied, given the circumstances of the offence, that the manner in which the accused dealt with the property or its proceeds is markedly unusual`
            OR `the court is satisfied, given the circumstances of the offence, that the accused’s dealings are inconsistent with lawful activities typical of the sector in which they take place, including business activities`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may infer that an accused had the knowledge or belief or demonstrated the recklessness referred to in subsection (1) if it is satisfied"

-- src:8025 | (2.4) Subsections (2.2) and (2.3) do not apply in cases where the accused is also charged with the designated offence.
@ref s 462.31(2.4) (src:8025)
GIVEN `the accused is also charged with the designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.31(2.4) subsections (2.2) and (2.3) do not apply` MEANS
    IF `the accused is also charged with the designated offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in cases where the accused is also charged with the designated offence"

-- src:8027 | (3) A peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer is not guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2.1) if the peace officer or person does any of the things mentioned in that subsection for the purposes of an investigation or otherwise in the execution of the peace officer’s duties.
@ref s 462.31(3) (src:8027)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer or person does any of the things mentioned in subsection (1) or (2.1) for the purposes of an investigation or otherwise in the execution of the peace officer’s duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.31(3) the person is not guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2.1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer`
        AND `the peace officer or person does any of the things mentioned in subsection (1) or (2.1) for the purposes of an investigation or otherwise in the execution of the peace officer’s duties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer is not guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2.1) if"
